{"title":"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Inequalities)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Inequalities)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A box contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> chips, numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Chips are drawn randomly one at a time without replacement until the sum of the values drawn exceeds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> draws are required?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/8/e987a6aadf83f1190380e2353a5b11f0568f6062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\frac{1}{15} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)} \\frac{1}{10} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)} \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)} \\frac{1}{5} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)} \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"358\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the only four ways such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> draws are required are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d338f393d100febd19e4284537ac40517b48340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c44bd27931d72780474233e818b567de93a7ffa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a78ef4dbb3e6ba13dc2581d27e7d0e0c66c4a017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16e9a931991c6c703de8abbc1f48a60bb6dfdaad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />. Notice that each of those cases has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/4/ba4284d43bade818970a4516a2524f69ed9d299b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"37\" height=\"37\" /> chance, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b13a01b3e89cca14caefd13030ee353f4a1869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 4 = \\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>Jonathan Xu (pi_is_delicious_69420)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1\">Solution 1.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since our favorable outcomes are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d338f393d100febd19e4284537ac40517b48340.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c44bd27931d72780474233e818b567de93a7ffa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a78ef4dbb3e6ba13dc2581d27e7d0e0c66c4a017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16e9a931991c6c703de8abbc1f48a60bb6dfdaad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />, we have 4 favorable outcomes. We have 20 total outcomes. Probability will be  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d129a7b3c0bf9fbd0693afdd426a66d2a0a8c3ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~east999\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We only have to analyze the first two draws as that gives us insight into if a third draw is necessary. Also, note that it is necessary to draw a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to have 3 draws, otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will be attainable in two or fewer draws. So the probability of getting a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d129a7b3c0bf9fbd0693afdd426a66d2a0a8c3ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. It is necessary to pull either a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the next draw and the probability of that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. But, the order of the draws can be switched so we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/9/3a95d1a33fcd51f5f29083cab5f0e2da3df77afb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 = \\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"97\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/5/3d543534cd2ead9a8dbdf64a3ff3beda948affc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"27\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>~Soccer_JAMS\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Inequalities.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Inequalities)\">Solution 3 (Inequalities)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Inequalities)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> draws must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/5/3e5079bced67d5e79255d65a2ffca3f904a0897e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> leaving us with with the only option being that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are chosen in either order. This means there is a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9af6b5ef87f022b38a2ccf4d6bfed09a58a5fb6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\binom52} \\cdot 2 = \\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"88\" height=\"46\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/5/3d543534cd2ead9a8dbdf64a3ff3beda948affc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"27\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>~MC_ADe\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gtsDrM16J9U\">https://youtu.be/gtsDrM16J9U</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ctQ3VbKAFBg\">https://youtu.be/ctQ3VbKAFBg</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wopflrvUN2c?t=20\">https://youtu.be/wopflrvUN2c?t=20</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B\">2018 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=